{"sha":"5f433377139a6eeaeacbdc894b70f8805b72c8b5","node_id":"C_kwDOMkQSetoAKDVmNDMzMzc3MTM5YTZlZWFlYWNiZGM4OTRiNzBmODgwNWI3MmM4YjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jim Bennett","email":"jim_bennett_home@hotmail.com","date":"2026-10-03T23:17:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"Jim Bennett","email":"jim_bennett_home@hotmail.com","date":"2026-10-03T23:17:51Z"},"message":"Version 0.2.1:\n\nFix issues from users, up to the limits of our current restriction to 'frame' years.\n\nSerbia-Montenegro becomes Republic of Serbia in 2006.\nDropped German Confederation shapes restored; now runs to 1866.\nDropped North German Confederation shapes restored; runs to 1870.\nDuchy of Warsaw separated from Kingdom of Saxony between 1814-1870.\nNorthern Song extended to 1127.\nMany corrections to clarify Africa's Gold Coast, Cape Coast, and Freetown Colony.\n- Dutch Gold Coast though 1871, then British Gold Coast through 1960.\n- Freetown Colony separated from Gold Coast and Cape Coast records.\nMis-labeled French Equatorial Africa polygons added to French Algeria 1842-1847.\nDanish India and Danish Gold Coast records separated  properly between 1659-1852.\nFixed Portugal's overseas possessions missing MemberOf association with the Portuguese Empire after 1823.\n\nMany corresponding wikidata and a few wikipedia updates.","tree":{"sha":"21c824cf453d90b99fd58e20309a1dd2521db283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria/git/trees/21c824cf453d90b99fd58e20309a1dd2521db283"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria/git/commits/5f433377139a6eeaeacbdc894b70f8805b72c8b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria/commits/5f433377139a6eeaeacbdc894b70f8805b72c8b5","html_url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria/commit/5f433377139a6eeaeacbdc894b70f8805b72c8b5